From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:42:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: Add the VXD stateless H.264 decoder
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Apple A9 (S8000/S8003) VXD block is an Imagination PowerVR MSVDX
decoder whose MTX microcontroller runs Apple's DEVA firmware. Linux on
the iPad 5 has no hardware video decoding without it.

Add a V4L2 stateless H.264 decoder for it, following the iOS 16.7.10
AppleD5500 kext:

- probe reads the core identity, sets up the core's own two-level GART
  (there is no DART) and registers the m2m video and media devices;
- the DEVA firmware (apple/vxd-deva.bin) boots in AppleD5500's order:
  PrepareCore, LoadFirmwareAndStartCore, the ready magic, the ring
  geometry and the 0x80 init message;
- the host and the firmware talk through two message rings in the
  register file; decode packets complete with a 0xc0 message carrying
  the fence;
- per picture the driver parses the slices of the Annex-B access unit,
  builds RefPicList0/1, resolves the DPB to CAPTURE buffers and writes
  the MSVDX command stream into one of eight GART-mapped command
  buffers, submitted one mailbox message per slice.

The firmware boots on the first open of the video node rather than at
probe: built in, the driver probes before the root filesystem with the
firmware file is mounted, and open is the first point where a decoder
is needed. It keeps running, and the block powered, until the driver is
unbound. This follows other m2m decoders that load firmware on first
open (mtk-vcodec).

Device result on J71t: H.264 High, B-frames, weighted prediction,
scaling lists and multi-slice pictures decode bit-exact; 1080p decodes
300/300 frames at 52.8 fps.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux b4d792c0 (J71t ledger 12.1) and
 omarchy-ipad5 patches/vdec/round1-7; the bring-up staging is removed:
 the dev_emerg STEP lines (and the pr_flush they needed), the
 boot_firmware, va_offset, debug, v4l2, step_ioctls and scaling_order
 parameters, the debugfs boot/ping/consume_check triggers and dumps, the
 probe-time self-tests and the PMGR state logging. The firmware boots on
 first open instead of through the parameter or debugfs. capture_cached
 is replaced by the standard V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT cache hint;
 the firmware SHA-256 check is dropped (the firmware recipe pins it).]
